# Line endings are LF, in the repository and in every checkout.
#
# Without this a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true holds CRLF, while
# MSYS2's git -- which has autocrlf off -- reads that same worktree as though
# every line of every file had been rewritten: 120 files, 33680 insertions,
# 33680 deletions. tools/package.sh asks git whether the tree is clean, so the
# packages it built on Windows were all stamped "-dirty" and their BUILD.txt
# claimed "WITH UNCOMMITTED CHANGES" against a checkout nobody had touched.
#
# The two gits have to agree, and LF is what the repository already stores.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The cartridge is bytes, not text. git works this out for itself -- see
# `git ls-files --eol`, which reports -text -- but only from a NUL byte in the
# first 8 KiB, and being wrong here would corrupt the dump silently until
# verify-rom caught it.
*.bin -text
